From: AlphaWRT
Subject: net: airoha: npu: read AN7581 IRQs in device tree order

The AN7581 binding lists the mailbox, the core watchdogs, then the WLAN lines.
Probe read WLAN right after the mailbox, so it ran off the end of the list with
"IRQ index 15 not found" and the NPU never started.

diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c	2026-11-02 01:26:54.624674344 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c	2026-11-02 01:26:54.642106896 +0800
@@ -1933,9 +1933,11 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	/* WLAN IRQ lines follow the mailbox IRQ on both NPU revisions. */
+	/* WLAN IRQ lines follow the mailbox on NPU v1, the watchdogs on v2 */
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(npu->irqs); i++) {
-		irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, i + 1);
+		irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, i + 1 +
+				       (npu->soc_data->version < NPU_V2 ? 0 :
+					npu->soc_data->max_cores));
 		if (irq < 0)
 			return irq;
 
@@ -1965,7 +1967,7 @@
 		if (npu->soc_data->version < NPU_V2)
 			continue;
 
-		irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, i + npu->soc_data->max_cores + 1);
+		irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, i + 1);
 		if (irq < 0)
 			return irq;
 
